Sorry I lost track of this:

@johannhof: Did y'all have a chance to analyze data from Firefox's telemetry?
@mthiesse: Do you know if we have metrics for this in Chromium?

@ydogandjiev Thanks!
Both Firefox and Safari enabled it. I am going to [enable it by default ](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/3596322) in Chrome today for M103 as it was scheduled.

I still see: [https://teams.microsoft.com](https://www.google.com/url?sa=D&q=https%3A%2F%2Fteams.microsoft.com) and [https://teams.live.com](https://www.google.com/url?sa=D&q=https%3A%2F%2Fteams.live.com) to be the two top impacted websites on 2022-04-17 by far. M103 canary users will start to be blocked in 2-3 days after I land the [patch](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/3596322). Please let me know if anything.
